        "original_id": "3122d151-36b1-558b-8bf2-fb01f65cd36a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: American Scientist, Dwell, Global Open Access Forum\n- Organizations: Sigma Xi, The Scientific Research Society\n- People: Lara Hedberg Deam, Karrie Jacobs\n- Topics: open access, science and technology publishing, design\n\nFacts:\n- American Scientist has been published since 1913 by Sigma Xi, The Scientific Research Society.\n- The Global Open Access Forum was created in September 1998 by American Scientist, which is published by Sigma Xi, and it was originally called the September98-Forum.\n- Dwell was launched with a magazine in September 2000 by Lara Hedberg Deam to bridge the gap between design professionals and enthusiasts.\n- Karrie Jacobs was Dwell's Editor-in-Chief at its September 2000 launch.\n- American Scientist is an American bimonthly science and technology magazine and is informally abbreviated AmSci.",
